From 2a7bd1aed2818d280ba34384f8b893e358cf0e92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Bouzas <julian.bouzas@collabora.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 10:45:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] spa: alsa: recheck ACP profile-set on HDMI ELD changes

Currently, if the system starts with an HDMI stereo ELD device and later
switches to an HDMI surround ELD device, the surround profile is not listed
in the spa-device because the profile set is only probed during initialization.

This patch re-checks ACP HDMI profile availability when HDMI ELD data changes
at runtime, instead of relying only on the startup probe result.

The check parses the ELD file and verifies that its channel count matches the
one from the mapping.
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/pipewire/pipewire/-/commit/2a7bd1aed2818d280ba34384f8b893e358cf0e92
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-13
